{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-mf2p-h6hf-fcwm","published":"2026-10-27T21:07:12Z","modified":"2026-10-27T21:15:04.912450737Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-116675"],"summary":"TinyMCE Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability using media plugin `data-mce-object` serialization","details":"### Impact\nStored XSS vulnerability in the media plugin. Attackers can inject malicious scripts via elements crafted through the data-mce-object attribute, which are created and executed before sanitization. Impacts users of TinyMCE with the media plugin enabled.\n\n### Patches\nThis vulnerability has been patched in TinyMCE 8.9.3 and TinyMCE 7.9.4 by ensuring that, when using the media plugin, any content created through the data-mce-object attribute is properly sanitized first.\n\n### Workarounds\nNo official workaround available.\n\n### Fix\nTo avoid this vulnerability:\n\nUpgrade to TinyMCE 8.9.3 or higher.\nUpgrade to TinyMCE 7.9.4 or higher.\n\n### Acknowledgements\nTiny thanks [Fariskhi Vidyan](https://github.com/farisv) and David Vieira Kurz (HiSolutions AG) for their help identifying this vulnerability.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"tinymce","ecosystem":"npm","purl":"pkg:npm/tinymce"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"8.5.1"},{"fixed":"8.9.3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/10/GHSA-mf2p-h6hf-fcwm/GHSA-mf2p-h6hf-fcwm.json"}},{"package":{"name":"TinyMCE","ecosystem":"NuGet","purl":"pkg:nuget/TinyMCE"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"8.5.1"},{"fixed":"8.9.3"}]}],"versions":["8.5.1","8.6.0","8.7.0","8.8.0","8.8.1","8.8.2","8.9.0","8.9.1","8.9.2"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/10/GHSA-mf2p-h6hf-fcwm/GHSA-mf2p-h6hf-fcwm.json"}},{"package":{"name":"tinymce/tinymce","ecosystem":"Packagist","purl":"pkg:composer/tinymce/tinymce"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{